In most of these examples, replacing {lo broda} with {su'o broda} would give weird results.


   mi ze'a nonkansa secau __lo prenu poi mi ke'a ka'e tavla__
   ''I was alone for some time, without __anyone to talk to__.''

   mi zmadu __lo porpi bloti prenu noi cpana lo fultapla bu'u lo xamsi midju ku'o__ le ka sepli
   ''I was more isolated than __a shipwrecked sailor on a raft in the middle of the ocean__.''

   __lo makcu prenu__ mi tolxlu lo nu pirlarcu se jibri kei ca le nu mi nanca li xa
   ''__The grown-ups__ discouraged me in my painter's career when I was six years old.''

   __lo sincrboa__ cu mutce le ka ckape ije __lo xanto__ cu mutce le ka fanza
   ''__A boa constrictor__ is a very dangerous creature, and __an elephant__ is very cumbersome.''

   i mi nitcu __lo lanme__ i ko pirfi'i __lo lanme__ seva'u mi
   ''What I need is __a sheep__. Draw me __a sheep__.''

   mi djica __lo lanme poi ba ze'u jmive__
   ''I want __a sheep that will live a long time__.''

   ca __lo nicte__ ty selfu ly lo nu zdani
   ''At __night__ he uses it as his house.''

   ly jorne ze'a __lo donri__
   ''He is tied during __the day__.''

   le ny krasi plini cu ja'aru'e zmadu __lo zdani__ le ka barda
   ''The planet he came from was scarcely any larger than __a house__.''

   le ra patfu cu jerna __lo rupnu be li xo__
   ''__How much money__ does his father make?''

   ei __lo verba__ cu mutce fraxu __lo makcu prenu__
   ''__Children__ should always show great forbearance toward __grown-up people__.''

   ku'i uinai mi na viska __lo lanme__ pa'o __lo tanxe__ i ju'ocu'i mi milxe simsa __lo makcu prenu__
   ''But I, alas, do not see __sheep__ through the walls of __boxes__. Perhaps I am a little like __the grown-ups__.''
